   "note": "Stanza numbers moved into the section field.",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "By thinking of all sentient beings",
     "section": "Verse 1"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "As more precious than a wish-fulfilling jewel",
     "section": "Verse 1"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "For accomplishing the highest aim,",
     "section": "Verse 1"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "I will always hold them dear.",
     "section": "Verse 1"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "Whenever I’m in the company of others,",
     "section": "Verse 2"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "I will regard myself as the lowest among all,",
     "section": "Verse 2"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "And from the depths of my heart",
     "section": "Verse 2"
    },
    {
     "n": 8,
     "text": "Cherish others as supreme.",
     "section": "Verse 2"
    },
    {
     "n": 9,
     "text": "In my every action, I will watch my mind,",
     "section": "Verse 3"
    },
    {
     "n": 10,
     "text": "And the moment destructive emotions arise,",
     "section": "Verse 3"
    },
    {
     "n": 11,
     "text": "I will confront them strongly and avert them,",
     "section": "Verse 3"
    },
    {
     "n": 12,
     "text": "Since they will hurt both me and others.",
     "section": "Verse 3"
    },
    {
     "n": 13,
     "text": "Whenever I see ill-natured beings,",
     "section": "Verse 4"
    },
    {
     "n": 14,
     "text": "Or those overwhelmed by heavy misdeeds or suffering,",
     "section": "Verse 4"
    },
    {
     "n": 15,
     "text": "I will cherish them as something rare,",
     "section": "Verse 4"
    },
    {
     "n": 16,
     "text": "As though I’d found a priceless treasure.",
     "section": "Verse 4"
    },
    {
     "n": 17,
     "text": "Whenever someone out of envy",
     "section": "Verse 5"
    },
    {
     "n": 18,
     "text": "Does me wrong by attacking or belittling me,",
     "section": "Verse 5"
    },
    {
     "n": 19,
     "text": "I will take defeat upon myself,",
     "section": "Verse 5"
    },
    {
     "n": 20,
     "text": "And give the victory to others.",
     "section": "Verse 5"
    },
    {
     "n": 21,
     "text": "Even when someone I have helped,",
     "section": "Verse 6"
    },
    {
     "n": 22,
     "text": "Or in whom I have placed great hopes",
     "section": "Verse 6"
    },
    {
     "n": 23,
     "text": "Mistreats me very unjustly,",
     "section": "Verse 6"
    },
    {
     "n": 24,
     "text": "I will view that person as a true spiritual teacher.",
     "section": "Verse 6"
    },
    {
     "n": 25,
     "text": "In brief, directly or indirectly,",
     "section": "Verse 7"
    },
    {
     "n": 26,
     "text": "I will offer help and happiness to all my mothers,",
     "section": "Verse 7"
    },
    {
     "n": 27,
     "text": "And secretly take upon myself",
     "section": "Verse 7"
    },
    {
     "n": 28,
     "text": "All their hurt and suffering.",
     "section": "Verse 7"
    },
    {
     "n": 29,
     "text": "I will learn to keep all these practices",
     "section": "Verse 8"
    },
    {
     "n": 30,
     "text": "Untainted by thoughts of the eight worldly concerns.",
     "section": "Verse 8"
    },
    {
     "n": 31,
     "text": "May I recognize all things as like illusions,",
     "section": "Verse 8"
    },
    {
     "n": 32,
     "text": "And, without attachment, gain freedom from bondage.",
     "section": "Verse 8"
    }
   ]
  },
